From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rdoupe
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/24] Follow tailscaled's IPN bus instead of polling Tailscale status

Every 30 seconds each bar ran three tailscale clients: status, the exit-node
list and the account list, though the bar icon needs status alone and only
changes when Tailscale goes up or down or needs a login. Exit nodes and
accounts are fetched only when the panel opens and while it is open, on
refreshIntervalSec as before. With the panel closed nothing polls: one
`tailscale debug watch-ipn --initial` per panel follows tailscaled's IPN bus,
and status is refreshed only for a notification carrying a State, Prefs,
finished login, login URL or error. Any local user may watch the bus. The
watch dies with the shell (pdeathsig); when tailscaled stops or restarts it
refreshes once and reconnects, backing off from a second to a minute. A
refresh asked for while a status call runs is made again when it exits, so a
change that lands mid-call still reaches the icon.

Backport to v4.5.0-rc1: as on quattro; Panel.qml keeps upstream's
loadedContent focus call on open, and only the tailscale.refresh() call is
removed. Fork commits cf5cf22a, 2a1d84b0 and d3e137d8 on asus/v4-5-0-rc1,
squashed (perf/tailscale-poll a843b2b2 + 56579319 + 63d0a63a).

Backport to v4.5.0-rc2: v4.5.0-rc2 carries omacom/omarchy#7623, which polls status without peers while the panel is closed (peersWanted). The IPN-bus watch replaces that poll. The open panel's full refresh, every peer included, moves from Panel.qml's open handler to onPanelOpenChanged, so exit nodes and accounts load with it. A full-peer request made during a light call keeps #7623's pending rerun; any other request made mid-call reruns once the call ends.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
